[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Do You Call That a Hat?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.52]What kind of shopping does the writer enjoy, do you think? | 你认为作者喜欢什么样的购物？
[00:17.83]'Do you call that a hat?' I said to my wife. | “你把那个叫帽子吗？”我对妻子说。
[00:22.99]'You needn't be so rude about it,' | “你不必这么没礼貌，”
[00:26.28]my wife answered as she looked at herself in the mirror. | 我的妻子一边回答，一边照着镜子。
[00:31.68]I sat down on one of those modern chairs with holes in it and waited. | 我坐在一把新式的满是孔的椅子上等待着。
[00:37.94]We had been in the hat shop for half an hour and my wife was still in front of the mirror. | 我们在帽店里已经待了半个小时，而我的妻子仍在镜子前面。
[00:45.50]'We mustn't buy things we don't need,' I remarked suddenly. | “我们不应该买我们不需要的东西，”我突然发表意见说。
[00:51.39]I regretted saying it almost at once. | 我马上就后悔说了这句话。
[00:55.47]'You needn't have said that,' my wife answered. | “你没必要这么说，”我妻子回答说。
[00:59.98]'I needn't remind you of that terrible tie you bought yesterday.' | “我也无需提醒你昨天买的那条糟糕透了的领带。”
[01:05.85]'I find it beautiful,' I said. 'A man can never have too many ties.' | “我觉得它很好看，”我说，“男人有多少领带也不会嫌多。”
[01:13.40]'And a woman can't have too many hats,' she answered. | “而女人有多少帽子也不嫌多，”她回答说。
[01:19.07]Ten minutes later we walked out of the shop together. | 10分钟以后，我们一起走出了商店。
[01:23.84]My wife was wearing a hat that looked like a lighthouse! | 我妻子戴着一顶帽子，看起来像一座灯塔！
